-- title:
--   Patching data over the localised Hecke algebra, cube-free levels
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass model over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W\neq 0$ which is semistable in the sense that $q\mid\Delta_W$ implies $q\nmid c_4(W)$ for every prime $q$, and whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible in the sense that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Assume $W$ is residually modular of some level $M_0\ge 1$: there is a normalised weight-$2$ eigenform on $\Gamma_0(M_0)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$ such that for every prime $\ell\neq p$ with $\ell\nmid M_0$ and $\ell\nmid\Delta_W$ the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient is an algebraic integer congruent to $a_\ell(W)$ modulo $\mathfrak m$, where $a_\ell(W)=\ell+1-\#W(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction; assume further $p^2\nmid M_0$ and $q^3\nmid M_0$ for every prime $q\neq p$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$ and every prime dividing $\Delta_W$, and let $N\ge 1$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$, $q^2\mid N$ and $q^3\nmid N$ for all $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$, while $p\mid N$ and $p^2\nmid N$ if $p\mid\Delta_W$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$, and $p\nmid N$ if $p\nmid\Delta_W$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$. Assume the space $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by the forms with integral $q$-coefficients, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for all such $\ell$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}'$, again a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, with $\mathcal{O}\to\mathcal{O}'$ local and injective, such that, writing $\theta'$ for $\theta$ followed by the induced map of residue fields and $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪' θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) for the corresponding localisation of the $\mathcal{O}'$-Hecke algebra, there is an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $T\to\mathcal{O}'$, and moreover: for every proof that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has cardinality $p^2$, every proof that the mod $p$ Galois action factors through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, every ring homomorphism $\iota$ from $\mathbb{Z}/p$ to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$, and every datum $H$ of type [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for $N$, $S$, $\mathcal{O}'$, $\theta'$ with $T$ as its Hecke-module ring, both of the following hold, with $\bar\rho$ the residual representation on the $p$-torsion of $W$ base changed along $\iota$. First, if $p\mid\Delta_W$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$, then for every universal deformation datum $D$ for $\bar\rho$ and the ordinary condition [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪' p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28) (cyclotomic determinant, ordinary at $p$, unramified outside $S$), every local $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra map $\varphi\colon D.R\to T$ whose base change of $D.\rho$ is equivalent to $H.\rho$, there are a nontrivial abelian group $M$ carrying a $D.R$-module and a $T$-module structure with $\varphi(x)\cdot m=x\cdot m$ for all $x$ and $m$, and an $r$ with a nonempty [`Algebra.PatchingDatum 𝒪' p r D.R M`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L39), that is, for every $n$ a patching level relative to the ideal generated by the $(1+X_j)^{p^n}-1$ in $\mathcal{O}'[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$. Second, the same conclusion holds when $p\nmid\Delta_W$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$, with the ordinary condition replaced by the flat condition [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪' p S`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47).
--
--   This is the output of the Taylor–Wiles patching construction in the form used for modularity lifting: it produces, after a finite extension of the coefficient ring, a patched module over the universal deformation ring and the localised Hecke algebra, in both the ordinary and the flat (good supersingular) case at $p$. It is the variant in which the residual-modularity witness level $M_0$ and the auxiliary level $N$ are cube-free away from $p$, and it feeds the subsequent bound on the length of the cotangent module of the Hecke algebra.
